message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example of a “rotating card” that spins 180° around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card container ---------- */
.card{
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    perspective:1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Card inner (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card-inner{
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform 0.8s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide the back face when turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Back face styling */
.card-back{
    background:#4a90e2;
    color:#fff;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* start rotated so it’s hidden */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me to see the back!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Thanks for hovering!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
1. **Perspective** – The `.card` container has `perspective:1000px;` which gives the 3D effect.
2. **Rotation** – The `.card-inner` element is the one that rotates.  
   - `transform-style: preserve-3d;` keeps its children in 3D space.
   - On hover, we apply `transform: rotateY(180deg);`.
3. **Faces** – Both `.card-front` and `.card-back` are absolutely positioned on top of each other.  
   - `backface-visibility:hidden;` hides the backside when it’s turned away.
   - The back face starts rotated 180° so it’s initially hidden.

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or transition timing to fit your design!
